\name{etr_plot_recurrence_rate_curve}
\alias{etr_plot_recurrence_rate_curve}
\title{Plot recurrence radius profile source scientific artists}
\usage{
etr_plot_recurrence_rate_curve(result, strict_source_record = FALSE, ...)
}
\arguments{
\item{result}{Native radius-profile result with declared metric and recurrence rate.}\item{strict_source_record}{Return native typed scientific artists when TRUE.}\item{...}{Legacy base R graphics options.}
}
\value{Native default invisibly returns the original radius/rate profile table. Strict mode provides the exact source radius line, markers, title and fixed y limits from zero to one.}
\description{Native scientific geometry for the frozen Python 1.2 nonlinear plotting contract. Scientific estimators and the default base R graphics return are unchanged.}
\details{The strict source record does not return a live Python Matplotlib Axes, accept arbitrary Python dataclasses, reproduce Python exception classes, or establish pixel parity. No independent full-contract certification is claimed.}
